# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caches and downloaded third-party material. NEVER commit these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cached API responses (_raw/) and raw page/PDF copies (raw/). The cached
# responses can contain publisher-author contact addresses, and the PDFs/HTML
# belong to their publishers, so neither can be redistributed.
_raw/
raw/
fulltext/
_ft/

# Downloaded paper PDFs (copyrighted; re-fetch with audit/fetch_oa_pdfs.py etc.)
*.pdf
# Downloaded XML/HTML full texts, saved next to whatever they came from
*.xml


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data outputs. Regenerable by re-running the scripts in this
# package (see README, "How to reproduce"); not redistributed here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/` is the default root every generated output resolves to (see paths.py)
data/
*.qs
*.tsv
*_resolved.json
*_ordered.json
*_cite_order.json
*.docx
*.doc
output/
outputs/
out/
build-artifacts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient session scratch and one-off probes. The curation rule behind this
# package (README, "Curation rule") keeps these OUT of the published tree; they
# are listed here so a stray probe cannot be committed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.probe-*
.*probe*
zz-*
cf-probe*
cf-diag*
check-*.sh
wait-*.sh
watch-*.sh
*probe*.sh
why-died.sh
kill-*
stop-*
_inspect/
_stage/
scratch/
# sandbox used while verifying a patch: cloned upstream repo + before/after files.
# Never publish it (it carries third-party sources and author metadata).
.verify/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEGATIONS -- load-bearing, and deliberately LAST: in .gitignore the last
# matching rule wins, and the broad `*.tsv` / `*.pdf` rules above would
# otherwise silently drop these. Without them a plain `git add .` leaves out
# the per-dataset mappings and the harness cannot run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!harness/benchmark/*/mapping.tsv
!figures/*.pdf
figures/
supplementary/
